%% FLOW-02: Ingestion (загрузка резюме)
%% Source: architecture/KNOWLEDGE_MAP.md — Flows
%% Updated: 2026-02-15 - added block-wise translation and semantic parsing with metadata

sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    participant Client
    participant Gateway as API Gateway
    participant RabbitMQ
    participant Ingestion as Ingestion Service
    participant Translation as Translation Service
    participant Embedding as Embedding Service
    participant Qdrant
    participant DB as PostgreSQL

    Client->>Gateway: upload document
    Gateway->>RabbitMQ: publish upload_document
    RabbitMQ->>Ingestion: consume command
    
    Note over Ingestion: split_resume_sections(general, experience)
    Note over Ingestion: split_experience_by_companies()
    
    par Parallel translation (up to MAX_THREAD_WORKERS)
        Ingestion->>Translation: POST /translate (general ru→en)
        Translation-->>Ingestion: general_en
    and
        Ingestion->>Translation: POST /translate (company 1 ru→en)
        Translation-->>Ingestion: company_1_en
    and
        Ingestion->>Translation: POST /translate (company 2 ru→en)
        Translation-->>Ingestion: company_2_en
    and
        Ingestion->>Translation: POST /translate (company N ru→en)
        Translation-->>Ingestion: company_N_en
    end
    
    Note over Ingestion: Reconstruct: general + companies
    Note over Ingestion: Semantic parsing: extract metadata<br/>(company_name, date_range, project_name,<br/>project_domain, role)
    
    Ingestion->>DB: begin transaction, delete old version
    Ingestion->>DB: save document
    
    Note over Ingestion: chunks_from_semantic_resume()<br/>with metadata
    
    loop chunks with metadata
        Ingestion->>Embedding: embed_batch(chunks)
        Embedding-->>Ingestion: vectors
    end
    
    Ingestion->>Qdrant: write vectors + metadata payload
    Ingestion->>DB: write chunks + metadata
    Ingestion->>DB: commit
    Ingestion->>RabbitMQ: publish ingestion_results
    Ingestion-->>Client: (callback/optional) success
